================================================================================
1. FLEXNET ARCHITECTURE CODE (PERMITTED TEMPLATE USE)
================================================================================

FlexNet Architecture Code is licensed by Kit Baroness and includes:

  - The overall project structure and runtime pattern (shell + hash router +
    view fragments + ES module loader + frozen site config)
  - Files and folders whose primary purpose is runtime architecture, including
    but not limited to:
      src/core/loader.js
      src/core/site-config.js (structure and helper patterns, not site data)
      src/core/layout/
      src/utilities/
      src/views/ (module patterns and interaction logic, not site copy)
      css/styles.css (BEM component structure and layout patterns)
      scripts/serve.py
      scripts/check.sh
      _headers and _redirects (as deployment pattern examples)
      index.html shell markup and module bootstrap (not inline page content)
  - The example/ directory, when present, as reference material only

You MAY, for any purpose including commercial projects:

  - Use, copy, modify, and merge FlexNet Architecture Code
  - Create derivative works based on FlexNet Architecture Code
  - Use the code as a template or example for other static sites
  - Deploy sites built from FlexNet Architecture Code

You MUST:

  - Include a copy of this license (or a clear link to it) in any substantial
    redistribution of FlexNet Architecture Code
  - Retain attribution to Kit Baroness and the FlexNet JSX architecture in
    source files you copy verbatim, or in your project README / LICENSE if files
    are heavily rewritten
  - Replace site-specific branding, copy, images, and configuration with your
    own content before publishing a public site

You MAY NOT:

  - Remove or obscure FlexNet attribution from copied architecture files
  - Represent your project as an official FlexNet product or endorsement by
    Kit Baroness without written permission
  - Republish this repository, or a substantially unchanged copy of it, as a
    competing template marketplace product without written permission


